macbook12-audio-dkms for Debian 13 (trixie)
===========================================

What this is
------------
Out-of-tree HD-audio codec driver for the Cirrus Logic CS4208 codec of the
12-inch MacBook 9,1 (Early 2016) and MacBook 10,1 (2017), packaged with DKMS
for Debian 13. It replaces the in-kernel snd-hda-codec-cirrus module with a
version that replays the macOS codec initialization sequence, so the internal
speakers, the headphone jack, automatic jack switching and the internal
microphone work.

This package fixes the Debian-13-specific failures of the upstream
leifliddy/macbook12-audio-driver installer:

  * the DKMS prepare step rejected Debian kernel releases such as
    "6.12.115+deb13-amd64" ("Unsupported kernel release"),
  * it looked for a kernel source tarball that Debian never installs
    (Debian ships /usr/src/linux-source-6.12.tar.xz from the
    linux-source-6.12 package),
  * DKMS built for the running kernel instead of the target kernel,
  * the module BTF step failed because "pahole" was missing (Debian kernels
    enable BTF for modules).

The module was verified to compile, link and generate BTF against the
Debian 13 linux-headers-6.12.115+deb13-amd64 headers.

The package bundles the kernel sound/pci/hda sources (Linux 6.12.115),
so building does NOT require the ~1.5 GB linux-source-6.12 package.
If you want an exact source match with your running kernel, install
linux-source-6.12 and the build will use it automatically.

Installation
------------
Kernel headers are needed to build the module; install them first if
they are not present yet:

    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install linux-headers-amd64 dwarves

Then install the package (installs cleanly even if some of the above
failed; the build step reports exactly what is missing):

    sudo apt install ./macbook12-audio-dkms_0.3_all.deb

(or: sudo dpkg -i macbook12-audio-dkms_0.3_all.deb)

The package builds the module for every installed kernel that has
headers during installation. Then reboot (or let the installer reload
the audio stack):

    sudo reboot

Required: speaker software volume (WirePlumber)
-----------------------------------------------
The internal speaker has NO usable hardware volume control (the codec's only
analog amplifier is wired to the headphone path). PipeWire must apply volume
in software, otherwise the speaker volume slider does nothing.

This package installs /etc/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/51-macbook-cs4208-softvol.conf
(WirePlumber 0.5+, which is what Debian 13 ships). If you use an older
WirePlumber 0.4, copy the Lua variant instead:

    sudo cp /usr/share/doc/macbook12-audio-dkms/examples/51-macbook-cs4208-softvol.lua \
            /etc/wireplumber/main.lua.d/
    sudo rm /etc/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/51-macbook-cs4208-softvol.conf

Then run:

    amixer -c0 sset Master 100% unmute
    sudo alsactl store
    systemctl --user restart wireplumber

(If your audio controller is not at PCI 00:1f.3, adjust device.name in the
config; find it with "wpctl status" or "pactl list cards short".)

Verifying
---------
    dkms status                     # macbook12-audio-driver/0.3, ...: installed
    modinfo snd-hda-codec-cirrus    # filename should contain /updates/
    aplay -l                        # should list the analog devices of card 0

Kernel updates
--------------
When you install a new kernel (linux-image + linux-headers), DKMS rebuilds
this driver automatically (AUTOINSTALL=yes). Nothing to do.

Troubleshooting
---------------
* Secure Boot: unsigned out-of-tree modules do not load with Secure Boot
  enabled. Either disable Secure Boot, or enroll a MOK for DKMS
  (see the dkms mok tools / Debian wiki "SecureBoot").

* Build failure: check /tmp/macbook12-audio-dkms.build.log, or run:

      dkms build -m macbook12-audio-driver -v 0.3 -k $(uname -r)

* "Linux kernel source not found": for 6.12.x kernels a bundled source
  snapshot is used automatically. For other kernel versions install the
  matching source package, e.g.:

      sudo apt install linux-source-6.12

* Custom kernel: point the build at the matching kernel source tarball:

      sudo MACBOOK12_AUDIO_KERNEL_SRC=/path/to/linux-6.12.x.tar.xz \
           dkms build -m macbook12-audio-driver -v 0.3 -k $(uname -r)

* "Module not found / still silent": make sure the module resolved to the
  out-of-tree copy:

      modinfo -n snd-hda-codec-cirrus     # must contain /updates/
      sudo depmod -a && sudo reboot

* Check the codec is seen at all:

      cat /proc/asound/card0/codec* | grep -i codec

  It should show "Cirrus Logic CS4208". If no codec is listed, the problem
  is at the controller level, not this driver.

Uninstall
---------
    sudo apt remove macbook12-audio-dkms

This removes the DKMS module and built .ko files. The in-kernel
snd-hda-codec-cirrus takes over again on the next reboot.

Source and rebuild
------------------
The driver sources live in /usr/src/macbook12-audio-driver-0.3/. This
package was built from a Debian source tree; rebuild with:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Upstream: https://github.com/leifliddy/macbook12-audio-driver
